\paragraph{Cartpole Swingup.} Cartpole Swingup (single-DoF locomotion) serves as a cross-environment control. Three seeds of the CIVO-trigger configuration (exp\_061: trained $e_{\dt}$, subsample ON, $H{=}8$, $\dt{=}2$) and three seeds of the no-embedding control (exp\_062) both produce zero CIVO onset. Despite using the hyperparameter combination that triggers collapse in all 10 tested multi-joint locomotion seeds (Walker/Cheetah), the single-joint Cartpole shows no CIVO, confirming the phenomenon requires multi-joint dynamics where temporal abstraction amplifies the reward fidelity gap.

