\paragraph{Mechanistic interpretation.}
The temporal ordering---embedding differentiation (${\sim}$20K) $\to$ reward fidelity gap (${\sim}$20K, \S\ref{sec:timeseries_fidelity}) $\to$ value overestimation (${\sim}$30K)---suggests a three-layer causal chain: the embedding first learns maximally differentiated representations that push $\dt{=}1$ and $\dt{=}2$ into opposite latent regions, the reward head then develops scale-dependent biases from these differentiated inputs, and the critic amplifies these biases through imagined rollout bootstrapping. The frozen embedding's constant near-zero cosine ($|\cos| < 0.2$) prevents the first link in this chain, explaining why freezing eliminates CIVO despite maintaining identical forward-pass architecture (\S\ref{sec:f3}).

